/* PHASE WIPE — user direction: "have my animation go first, then
   the other animation go. Right now it feels like another animation
   is playing over it."
   Solution: add a 20% pure-black HOLD at the start of the keyframe
   so the viewport sits fully black for ~260ms before the leading
   edge starts sweeping. That gives any concurrent animations
   (handDealIn stagger, banner slide, etc) ~260ms to do their early
   frames hidden behind black, then the wipe reveals everything in
   one continuous motion. Also bumped duration 1100ms → 1300ms for
   more drama. */
/* User feedback May-1: "There's still, like, a little bit of a pause.
   It looks like it stops and pauses." Root cause: the 20% black hold
   at the start (0-260ms of static viewport before the sweep began)
   was reading as a pause. Removed the hold so the bar sweeps from
   start to finish in one continuous motion, and switched to Material
   Design standard easing (0.4, 0.0, 0.2, 1.0) which is smoother than
   the previous symmetric 0.65/0/0.35/1 curve — gentle ease-out at
   both ends, constant velocity through the middle, no perceived
   stop/start anywhere along the path. */
@keyframes rlPhaseWipeSweep {
  0%   { transform: translate3d(-50%, 0, 0); }
  100% { transform: translate3d(50%, 0, 0); }
}
.rl-phase-wipe::before {
  animation: rlPhaseWipeSweep 1100ms cubic-bezier(0.4, 0, 0.2, 1) forwards !important;
}

